      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture of the test. The class contains only one actual test method (`test_badDates`) but is cluttered with 12 unused data provider methods and many unused imports. I'll improve understandability by:\n1. Removing all unused data provider methods (dead code in this class)\n2. Removing all unused imports\n3. Grouping and annotating `data_badDates()` rows by invalid-input categoryThe improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes 12 unused data provider methods and all unused imports, then reorganizes `data_badDates()` with category comments that explain each group of invalid inputs (non-leap-year St. Tib's Day, invalid month values, invalid day-of-month values, etc.), while keeping the test method and all 15 test cases identical to the original."
